# Topic-specific points per module (order: customer, rules, offer, operations, safety, people, money, growth). Check current official texts.
DEEP = {
"Internet Companies": ["Split users into buyers, sellers and browsers; measure each separately, since they leave for different reasons.","Online sellers must show clear identity, price, delivery time and return rights; PIX is the main local payment method, so plan for it.","Make the first purchase possible in under 2 minutes on a mid-range phone with weak signal.","Track the funnel: visit, search, cart, pay, deliver, review. Fix the step with the largest drop first.","Protect accounts: strong sign-in, rate limits, and a tested breach-response plan with a named contact.","Support in Portuguese with a reply promise (for example 4 working hours) and a written tone guide.","Watch customer acquisition cost against contribution per order; stop spend where payback exceeds 3 months.","Grow by repeat purchase: reminders, bundles and referrals before paid ads."],
"IT": ["Segment by size: micro offices want a fixed monthly plan, mid-size firms want response times in writing.","Contracts should state scope, response and fix times, backup duty, and data handling under LGPD.","Offer three plans (basic, standard, extended hours) with a clear list of what each covers.","Run a ticket log with category, time to first reply, time to fix, and root cause per ticket.","Keep tested offline backups and run a restore drill every quarter.","Train engineers on a runbook: the first 15 minutes of any outage are scripted.","Price by device or user per month; check that the top 3 clients are under 40% of income.","Move from fixing to preventing: monthly health reports reduce tickets and prove value."],
"Health": ["Describe the person by need: prevention, a chronic condition, or recovery; each has a different service rhythm.","Health services answer to the national health surveillance agency (ANVISA) and professional councils; confirm the licence for your service before advertising.","Offer care pathways with a clear first visit, follow-up date and a plain written plan.","Use a consent and records routine: identity check, history, plan, signature, secure storage.","Apply infection control: hand hygiene, cleaning logs, waste separation.","Train all staff in basic life support and refresh yearly.","Track no-show rate and average visit length; they decide how many visits fit a day.","Grow through referral relationships with other registered professionals, never through miracle claims."],
"Real Estate": ["Know three client types: first-time buyer, investor, and tenant. Each needs a different checklist.","Agents must hold a registration with the real estate professional council (CRECI); check the title at the registry office before any offer.","Offer a transparent file: title, taxes, debts, condominium rules, and an honest valuation range.","Run each deal through a stage list: enquiry, visit, offer, due diligence, contract, registry, handover.","The main risk is a defective title or hidden debt: verify the registry, tax and condominium records in writing.","Train agents to explain costs: transfer tax, registry fees, broker commission, in plain words.","Commission income arrives late; keep a cash cushion of three months of fixed cost.","Grow through reputation: after every closed deal, ask for a short written review and a referral."],
"Food": ["Pick a channel first: retail shelf, restaurant supply or direct online; each sets pack size and price.","Food firms register premises and products with the health surveillance bodies; labels need ingredients, allergens, batch and expiry.","Design the pack so the label, shelf life and storage advice answer the first customer question.","Keep a batch record: supplier lots in, process temperatures, lots out, so a recall can be traced in hours.","Use hazard analysis and critical control points: list hazards, set limits, monitor, record, correct.","Train every handler on hygiene, allergen separation and cleaning; sign-off before first shift.","Compute cost per case including waste of at least 3%; prices set without waste lose money quietly.","Grow with a second pack size or channel only after rejections fall below 1%."],
"Energy": ["Customer groups: homes, small firms, and large users; the buying driver is bill reduction, reliability, or both.","Electrical work must follow the national installation standard and use certified equipment; the energy regulator (ANEEL) sets rules for connection to the grid.","Offer a sized design with expected yearly savings shown as a range, not a promise.","Follow a work order: survey, design, approval, install, test, commission, handover pack.","Lock-out and tag-out before any work on live circuits; test for dead with a proven tester.","Train electricians on testing, earthing and working at height; keep their licences current.","Quote with a margin on materials and labour; include a 5% contingency and the cost of grid approval time.","Grow through maintenance contracts that keep systems producing and customers calling."],
"Oil & Gas": ["Customers are operators and contractors who buy on safety record first, price second.","The sector regulator (ANP) and environmental bodies set licensing; contractors must show insurance, training and audit records.","Offer a service package with scope, crew, equipment, permits and a safety plan in one file.","Use a permit-to-work system: no hot work, confined space or lifting without a signed permit.","Run job safety analysis before each task and stop-work authority for every worker.","Certify workers for height, confined space, firefighting and first aid; track expiry dates.","Cost every job with standby, travel and inspection time; late payment is common, so check credit terms.","Grow by passing audits: a clean record is the best sales tool."],
"Telecom": ["Describe the subscriber by use: home streaming, business voice and data, or mobile only; map coverage gaps by neighbourhood.","The telecom regulator (ANATEL) licenses services and approves equipment; check authorisation before selling or installing.","Offer a plan with real measured speeds, a clear price and no hidden charges.","Plan the network: sites, backhaul, power, spares; monitor links and alarms around the clock.","Protect tower and cabinet work with fall protection, electrical isolation and radio-frequency exposure limits.","Train field crews on splicing, testing and customer-home etiquette.","Monitor revenue per user, churn, and cost per site; churn above 3% a month needs a fix.","Grow by densifying where the coverage map shows demand, not by guessing."],
"Smart Home Builder": ["Ask families what they want to stop doing by hand; start with lighting, security or energy.","Wiring follows national electrical standards; devices need certification; keep manual control for every key function.","Offer three packages with a plain control panel that every family member can use.","Plan cable routes during construction; retrofit costs far more than first-fit.","Test every scene and fail-safe: what happens when the network or power is off.","Train installers to hand over with a one-page guide and a 20-minute family walkthrough.","Price hardware, install and a support plan separately; subscriptions must be clearly stated.","Grow by finished showcase homes and builder partnerships."],
"Road & Bridge Development": ["The client is a public or private owner who buys on cost, time and safety record.","Public works follow procurement rules; engineers must be registered with the engineering council (CREA).","Offer a work package: survey, design, materials plan, programme, quality plan, safety plan.","Use stage control: set out, earthworks, sub-base, base, surfacing, with tests before each next layer.","Traffic management and excavation shoring are the highest risks; plan and inspect daily.","Train gangs on plant safety, signalling and manual handling; keep a competent person on site.","Cash flow depends on measurement and certification; keep claims clean and dated.","Grow by delivering on time with documented quality, which wins the next tender."],
"Automated Farming Equipment": ["Farm owners buy when a machine saves labour in a short season; measure hectares and hours.","Machines need safety guards and operator training; import and certification rules apply.","Offer sale or hire, with a seasonal service plan and spare-parts kit.","Run a pre-season service and a daily check: fluids, guards, sensors, software.","Rotating parts, hydraulics and autonomous movement are the key hazards; use exclusion zones and stop buttons.","Train operators in short field sessions with a practical test.","Compare cost per hectare with hand labour; show payback in seasons.","Grow through cooperative sharing and local service points."],
"Construction Safety Management": ["Site owners buy to avoid stoppages, injuries and fines; list each site's top three hazards.","National construction safety rules (NR-18 and related) set duties for training, protection and inspection; confirm the current text.","Offer a package: risk plan, daily checks, training, audit and monthly report.","Run a daily start-of-shift talk, a weekly inspection and a monthly audit; log every finding with owner and date.","Falls, trench collapse, electrical contact and lifting are the leading causes; prioritise controls for these.","Train and certify site staff; keep records visible on site.","Price per site month with a clear audit schedule; track findings closed on time.","Grow by showing falling incident rates on client sites."],
"Sensor Manufacture": ["Customers are machine makers and plants who need accuracy and long-term stability.","Products may need conformity marking and metrology checks; keep calibration traceable to a recognised standard.","Offer a datasheet with range, accuracy, drift and operating limits, and a calibration certificate.","Calibrate against a reference at several points, record the result, and age-test samples from each batch.","Electrostatic damage and soldering fumes are hazards; use grounded benches and extraction.","Train technicians on handling, soldering to a standard, and test procedure.","Include yield loss and rework in unit cost; scrap above 5% is a warning.","Grow by publishing honest drift data and offering recalibration."],
"Internet Infrastructure": ["Customers need uptime numbers, location and support; list their critical systems.","Operators must meet data protection duties and keep access logs; check any licence needed for services you resell.","Offer service levels with uptime percentage, credit rules and response times.","Monitor power, cooling, links and capacity; record each incident with root cause.","Fire, power failure and physical access are core risks; test generators and suppression systems on schedule.","Train staff on change control: no change without a plan, a back-out and a window.","Plan capacity ahead; power and cooling decide how many racks you can sell.","Grow by adding redundancy and certifications that large buyers ask for."],
"International Trade": ["Match a buyer's exact need and market rules before you quote; verify the buyer exists.","Customs, classification codes, export licences and tax treatment apply; use a licensed customs broker where required.","Offer terms using recognised delivery terms so cost and risk transfer are clear.","Follow the order: quote, contract, payment security, production, inspection, shipping, customs, payment.","Payment default and rejected goods are main risks; use secured payment and pre-shipment inspection.","Train staff on documents: invoice, packing list, certificate of origin, transport document.","Include freight, insurance, duties and exchange-rate movement in the price.","Grow by repeating with one buyer well before adding many."],
"Tourist Automation": ["Visitors want times, prices and directions at the moment of need; local operators want fuller schedules.","Operators need correct registration; listings must show true prices and cancellation rules.","Design the tool around one task: find, book and pay in three screens.","Keep listings live: availability, price and opening hours checked daily.","Avoid sending a visitor to a closed or unsafe place; verify listings and report errors fast.","Train local partners to update listings and answer messages the same day.","Earn per booking; track commission after payment fees and refunds.","Grow with local content and honest reviews; remove poor performers."],
"Online / AI Investment Management": ["Know the saver: goal, time, and how much loss they can bear, before any suggestion.","Investment advice and portfolio management are regulated by the securities regulator (CVM); confirm the licence needed before offering.","Present risk and cost in plain terms; no promises of returns.","Keep a record of each client profile, advice, consent and review date.","Test models on past data and on bad periods; log every model change.","Train staff to explain, not sell; compliance review of all client messages.","Revenue is a fee; fixed costs for data and compliance can be heavy; test the break-even.","Grow through trust: clear reports and education before products."],
"Universities": ["Define the learner and the employer outcome in one line per programme.","Higher education programmes are authorised and evaluated by the national education authorities; check recognition before enrolment.","Design from outcomes backwards: task, condition, standard, then assessments, then lessons.","Run a term calendar with teaching, assessment and moderation; keep student records safe.","Academic integrity and student welfare are risks; set clear policies and support routes.","Train teaching staff in assessment design and feedback.","Cost per student includes staff, space, and platform; compare with fee-free alternatives when the learner pays nothing.","Grow through employer projects and graduate tracking."],
"Technical & Vocational Schools": ["Interview local employers: which skills do they hire for within six months?","Programmes should align with national technical education frameworks; confirm recognition of the certificate.","Plan 70% practice; each unit ends in a task done on real equipment to a standard.","Schedule workshop time so each learner gets enough hands-on hours.","Tool safety and workshop supervision are first; guard machines and limit group size.","Train instructors in demonstration, feedback and assessment.","Equipment costs dominate; plan maintenance and sharing.","Grow through employer placements and tracked job outcomes."],
"Sustainability Management": ["Customers want to cut cost and prove claims; start with one site and its bills.","Environmental licences and reporting duties apply; avoid claims that cannot be proven.","Offer a baseline, a target, a plan and a yearly report.","Measure energy, water, waste and emissions monthly; use the same method each time.","Greenwashing is the key risk; every claim needs data and a source.","Train site champions to read meters and log data.","Show payback of each measure in months.","Grow by publishing verified results and repeating the cycle."],
"Drones": ["Customers want data, not flights: crop health maps, roof checks, site progress.","Flights follow the aviation authority rules (ANAC and the airspace control body); register the aircraft and pilot where required and respect no-fly zones.","Offer a deliverable with accuracy, format and turnaround time.","Plan each job: site check, airspace check, weather, battery, flight plan, data check.","Loss of link, low battery and flying near people are key hazards; set return-to-home and keep distance.","Train pilots with logged hours and emergency drills.","Cost includes insurance, batteries and data processing time.","Grow by repeat monitoring contracts."],
"Distribution Companies": ["List retailers by order size and delivery windows; the shortest windows decide your routes.","Invoicing, tax documents and vehicle rules apply; keep proof of delivery for each drop.","Offer fixed delivery days and a minimum order that pays for the route.","Pick, load, route, deliver, collect proof, reconcile; count stock at every hand-over.","Short deliveries, damage and driver fatigue are main risks; set limits and log hours.","Train drivers and loaders on safe lifting and checking.","Track cost per drop and per kilometre.","Grow by adding drops per route before adding vehicles."],
"Package Delivery Services": ["Senders care about price and tracking; receivers care about time and safe hand-over.","Couriers follow transport and traffic rules; riders need protective gear and valid papers.","Offer clear tiers: same day, next day, economy, with scanning at each hand-over.","Cluster addresses by zone and set cut-off times to fill routes.","Road injury and parcel theft are key risks; train on safe riding and secure drop.","Pay and schedule riders fairly; review fatigue and incidents.","Know cost per parcel and drops per hour; failed deliveries erase profit.","Grow with dense zones and return handling."],
"Renewable Energy for Homes, Offices, Malls, Multiplexes": ["Segment by building type and roof or land available; bill history shows the size.","Grid connection follows the energy regulator rules; installations need certified equipment and qualified electricians.","Offer a sized system with a clear range of expected generation and payback.","Follow a survey, design, approval, install, commissioning and monitoring sequence.","Work at height and DC electrical hazards need fall protection and isolation procedures.","Train installers on mounting, wiring, testing and fire safety.","Show payback from bill savings after maintenance and inverter replacement.","Grow through maintenance and monitoring contracts."],
"Sports": ["Players, parents and clubs want progress, safety and fun; set goals per group.","Coaches should hold the relevant registration and first-aid training; check venue rules.","Offer a season plan with sessions, tests and feedback.","Plan each session: warm-up, skill, game, cool-down, record.","Injury risk from overload; set age-appropriate load and rest.","Train coaches in safeguarding children and basic life support.","Cost per session includes space, kit and coach; track attendance.","Grow through community events and visible player progress."],
"Brand Management": ["Interview customers on what they say about you; list the words they use.","Respect trademark rules: register the name and check for conflicts before use.","Write a promise, three proof points, a tone and a visual guide.","Apply the brand consistently on every touch point with a one-page checklist.","Risk of promising what operations cannot deliver; align promises with proof.","Train staff to use the brand guide and handle complaints in its tone.","Track recall and preference with a simple survey and sales lift.","Grow by consistent repetition and customer stories."],
"Travel Agencies": ["Travellers buy trust: clear plan, clear price, support.","Tourism providers follow registration and consumer-protection rules; check supplier licences.","Offer package options with every cost line and cancellation rule shown.","Book, confirm, document, brief, travel, follow up; track every supplier confirmation.","Supplier failure and health emergencies are risks; hold emergency contacts and insurance advice.","Train agents on visas, insurance and handling disruptions.","Know margin per trip and deposits held; keep client money separate.","Grow through repeat travellers and group trips."],
"Microgreens Farming": ["Chefs buy by freshness and consistency; ask for weekly volumes and delivery times.","Small producers register the business and follow food safety guidance for fresh produce; keep a water source test.","Offer a weekly standing order of defined tray sizes, three varieties, and a sample.","Cycle: soak, sow, blackout, light, water, harvest in 7 to 14 days; record each tray.","Mould and contaminated water are main risks; use clean seed, airflow and sanitised trays.","Train staff on hygiene and a harvest quality check.","Compute cost per tray including seed, medium, power and labour; check yield per rack.","Grow by adding shelves before adding rooms."],
"Care for Disabled and Elderly People": ["Start with the person: abilities, preferences, routines, and the family's role.","Care services follow social and health authority rules; check registration, staff checks and complaint routes.","Write a care plan the person and family agree and sign.","Daily routine: medication prompt, meals, mobility, hygiene, activity; log each visit.","Falls, medication errors and neglect are core risks; use checklists and two-person checks.","Train carers in safe lifting, dignity, dementia basics and emergency response.","Rates per day or hour; staff cost dominates; watch overtime.","Grow through family trust and good outcomes, not advertising claims."],
"Private Medicare": ["Patients choose by waiting time, trust and cost; map the payer mix.","Clinics need health authority licences and registered clinicians; billing to health plans follows regulator rules (ANS).","Offer a clear fee list and appointment promise.","Flow: booking, check-in, consult, tests, follow-up, billing; one record per patient.","Misdiagnosis, infection and billing errors are risks; peer review and audit.","Train front desk and clinicians on privacy and consent.","Collect from plans and patients; track denied claims and days to pay.","Grow by waiting time and outcome measures."],
"Home Security and Monitoring Services": ["Customers want to feel safe at a fair monthly price; map neighbourhood risks.","Installers follow electrical standards; monitoring involves personal data, so follow LGPD and clear consent.","Offer a package with sensors, a siren, a phone alert and a response plan.","Install, test every sensor, train the family, set a monitoring script.","False alarms waste trust; tune sensors and verify before dispatch.","Train technicians and operators on calm call handling.","Recurring revenue pays back equipment in months; track churn.","Grow by referrals from neighbours and building managers."],
"Language Schools": ["Test learner level and goal: work, study, travel, exams.","Language schools follow education and consumer rules; certificate claims must be true.","Design levels with can-do statements and a speaking task at the end of each.","Plan class: warm-up, input, practice, speaking, feedback, homework.","Learner drop-out is the risk; short cycles and attendance follow-up help.","Train teachers in feedback and error correction.","Know cost per class hour and seats filled.","Grow with levelled groups and exam preparation."],
"Courses for Foreigners": ["Newcomers need housing, work, banking and health vocabulary first.","Courses about residency should cite official sources and avoid legal advice.","Build scenarios: bank, clinic, rental, workplace, transport.","Run short blocks with role-play and local field visits.","Risk of outdated rules; date every fact and link to official pages.","Train teachers in plain language and cultural sensitivity.","Cost per learner and seats; discounts for groups from employers.","Grow through employer and community partnerships."],
"Construction and Technical Services": ["Describe the job by trade, size and urgency.","Work follows building codes and trade registrations; get written approvals where needed.","Quote with scope, materials, steps, timing and exclusions.","Job sheet: survey, quote, order, schedule, work, inspect, hand over.","Falls, electric shock and dust are core hazards; protective gear and isolation.","Train crews and supervise first jobs.","Quote with contingency; collect deposits and stage payments.","Grow by finishing on time and tidy sites."],
"Winery": ["Know buyers: shops, restaurants, wine clubs, and visitors.","Producers register with the agriculture authority (MAPA); labels follow wine rules.","Design range by style, price and story; keep a tasting sheet.","Cycle: harvest, crush, ferment, age, blend, bottle, label; log temperature and sulfite.","Spoilage, tank gas and press hazards; use ventilation and lockout.","Train cellar staff in hygiene and sampling.","Cost per bottle includes ageing time and losses.","Grow with club subscriptions and visits."],
}
